$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical Procedure for C-S Cross-Coupling Fe/Cg
(7 wt%, 162 mg) was added to a 25 mL flask, which was previously charged
with iodoarene (1.2 mmol), thiol (1 mmol) and KOH (2.0 equiv). Dry DMSO
(1.5 mL) was added while purging the flask with nitrogen. The round
bottom flask was purged once again and back filled with nitrogen and
heated in an oil bath at 125 °C for a period of 24 h after which the
flask was removed from the oil bath and allowed to come to r.t. Fe/Cg was
removed by ultracentrifugation at 8000 rpm. After which the reaction
mixture was poured into H2O (5 mL), and the aqueous layer was extracted
with EtOAc (3 × 10 mL). ( 4-chlorophenyl)(phenyl)sulfane( 3e ):3 1H NMR
(200 MHz, CDCl3, TMS): δ =7.40-7.22 (m, 7H), 7.16 (d, 2H, J = 8.5 Hz);
13C NMR (75MHz, CDCl3, TMS): δ = 135.4, 134.7, 132.1, 132.0, 131.4,
129.3, 127.5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, solid-supported catalyst, graphite-supported iron
catalyst used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
