$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of sulfone sulfideamidediamine (SSAD). Into a 100 mL,
three-necked, round-bottomed flask equipped with a Dean-Stark trap, a
condenser, a nitrogen inlet tube, a thermometer, an oil bath and a
magnetic stirrer were placed 0.01 mol of bis(4-chlorophenyl)sulfone, 25
mL of dry NMP, and 15 mL of dry toluene and 0.021 mol of AMPB. Then
0.0315 mol of K2CO3 was added to the mixture, and the reaction mixture
was heated to 140°C for 6 h with continuous stirring. The generated water
was removed from the reaction mixture by azeotropic distillation. The
reaction temperature was raised to 165°C by removing more toluene and
kept at the same temperature for 20 h. During this time, progress of the
reaction was monitored by thin-layer chromatography (TLC). The resulting
reaction mixture was cooled and poured into water. Then 100 mL of 3% NaOH
was added to the mixture, and the mixture was washed repeatedly with a 3%
NaOH solution and water. The obtained diamine was dried in a vacuum oven
at 60°C. Yield: 71%. IR (KBr, cm-1): 3345-3425, 1655, 1604, 1585, 1497,
1485, 1403, 1358, 1228, 1178, 1102, 1H-NMR (DMSO-d6, δ): 10.00 (s, 2H,
NH), 7.89 (d, 4H, phenyl), 7.71 (d, 4H, phenyl), 7.51 (d, 4H, phenyl),
7.20 (d, 4H, phenyl), 7.08 (d, 4H, phenyl), 6.62 (d, 4H, phenyl), 5.81
(s, 4H, amine). Elemental analysis: Calc. C 64.96, H 4.27, N 7.97. Found:
C 64.65, H 3.99, N 8.37.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, Dean-Stark trap used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Organosoluble, thermally stable polyamides containing sulfone and sulfide
units
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Mehdipour-Ataei, Shahram; Hatami, Mehdi; Mosslemin, Mohammad Hossein
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Chinese Journal of Polymer Science (2009), 27(6), 781-787

