$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2-Bromo-4-(4-nitrophenylsulfenyl)benzaldehyde (1, X = 4-NO2). To a
solution of 4-nitrobenzenethiol (3.1 g, 20 mmol),
2-bromo-4-fluorobenzaldehyde (4.1 g, 20 mmol) in DMF (40 mL) was added
K2CO3 (5.5 g, 40 mmol). The mixture was heated under nitrogen at 100 °C
overnight, then was cooled to room temperature, filtered through a short
pack of diatomaceous earth to remove the solid residue. The filtrate was
concentrated and poured into DCM (30 mL) and H2O (30 mL). The aqueous
phase was neutralized by addition of 3 M HCl, the layers were separated
and the aqueous phase was extracted with DCM (3 x 30 mL). The combined
organic extracts were washed with brine (30 mL), dried over MgSO4,
filtered and evaporated. The residue was purified by flash
chromatography, eluting with an EtOAc/heptanes gradient (0:100 to 100: 0)
to give compound 1 (X = 4-NO2) (4.3 g, 71%) as a fine yellow powder.
2-Bromo-4-(4-nitrophenylsulfenyl)benzaldehyde (1, X = 4-NO2), yield (4.3
g, 71%). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): 10.35 (s, 1H), 8.43 (dd, J = 2.3, 0.6
Hz, 1H), 7.98 (dd, J = 8.6, 2.3 Hz, 1H), 7.69-7.77 (m, 2H), 7.30 (dd, J =
8.6, 3.0 Hz, 1H), 7.12 (dd, J = 8.6, 0.8 Hz, 1H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective (in stage 1)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Discovery of Novel Benzoxaborole-Based Potent Antitrypanosomal Agents
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Ding, Dazhong; Zhao, Yaxue; Meng, Qingqing; Xie, Dongsheng; Nare, Bakela;
Chen, Daitao; Bacchi, Cyrus J.; Yarlett, Nigel; Zhang, Yong-Kang;
Hernandez, Vincent; Xia, Yi; Freund, Yvonne; Abdulla, Maha; Ang,
Kean-Hooi; Ratnam, Joseline; McKerrow, James H.; Jacobs, Robert T.; Zhou,
Huchen; Plattner, Jacob J.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM ACS Medicinal Chemistry Letters (2010), 1(4), 165-169

