$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 4,5-Bis(1-phenylethanethio)phthalonitrile
[Pn(SEtPh)2]. 1,2-Dichloro-4,5-nitrophthalonitrile (3.00 g, 15.2 mmol)
was dissolved in anhydrous THF (50 mL) under nitrogen atmosphere, and the
appropriate PhEtSH compound (6.20 g, 45.0 mmol) was added. After stirring
for 30 min, finely ground anhydrous potassium carbonate (9.75 g, 70.7
mmol) was added in portions over 1 h with efficient stirring. The
reaction mixture was stirred at 40 °C for 24 h under nitrogen atmosphere.
Then the solution was poured into ice water (200 mL). The precipitate was
filtered off, washed with water until the filtrate was neutral, and dried
in vacuo. Purification of the product was accomplished by silica gel
column chromatography (eluent: CHCl3:MeOH = 9:1). Rotary evaporation of
the solvent. Pn(SEtPh)2 as a colorless crystalline solid. (b)
(S)-Pn(SEtPh)2. Yield of the compound: 4.25 g (70.8% on the basis of
(S)-1,2-dichloro-4,5-nitrophthalonitrile); 1H NMR (300MHz, CDCl3) δ 1.65
(d, 3H, -CH3), 4.44 (q, 2H, S-CH-Ph), 7.14- 7.30 (m, 12H, -Ph and Ar);
13C NMR(75 MHz, CDCl3) δ 23.3, 47.2, 111.9, 115.4, 127.1, 128.3, 129.1,
131.8, 141.2, 144.2; FT-IR (KBr, cm-1) 3061, 3019, 2977, 2924, 2863, 2225
(C≡N), 1567, 1487, 1450, 1374, 1348, 1224 (C-S-C), 1102, 1058, 1022, 926,
765, 699, 525. Anal. Calcd for C24H20N2S2: C, 71.96; H, 5.03; N, 6.99%.
Found: C, 71.97; H, 5.27; N, 7.22%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
