$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Phthalonitriles 3b,d,f,h;
4,5-Di(2,3,4,6-tetra-O-acetyl-1-thio-β-D-glucopyranosyl)phthalonitrile
(3b); Typical Procedure Bu4NOH (14 mL, 20 mmol) was added to a mixture of
4,5-difluorophthalonitrile (2b; 1.64 g, 10 mmol) and
2,3,4,6-tetra-O-acetyl-1-thio-β-D-glucopyranose (1b; 7.29 g, 20 mmol) in
CH2Cl2 (20 mL). The reaction mixture was stirred at r.t. for 48 h,
diluted with H2O (200 mL) and extracted with CH2Cl2 (2 × 100 mL). The
combined organic phases were washed with H2O (200 mL), dried (MgSO4), and
concentrated in vacuo. The obtained syrup purified by column
chromatography over silica gel using toluene-acetone (5:1).
4,5-Di(2,3,6,2',3',4',6'-hepta-O-acetyl-1-thio-β-D-cellobiose)phthalonitrile
(3h). Prepared from
2,3,6,2',3',4',6'-hepta-O-acetyl-1-thio-β-D-cellobiose (1h, 2.60 g, 4
mmol) as described for compound 3b. Purification was carried out by
column chromatography using hexane-EtOAc (1:3) to afford 3h as a white
solid; yield: 2.02 g (71%). mp 275-280 °C; [α]D20 -58.6 (c 0.5, CHCl3).
1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 7.83 (s, 2 Harom), 5.19 (t, J4',3' = 5.1 Hz,
2 H, H-4'), 5.12 (t, J2,1 = 10.2 Hz, 2 H, H-2), 5.10-4.96 (m, 4 H, H-2',
H-3), 4.89 (t, J3',4' = 5.1 Hz, 2 H, H-3'), 4.75 (d, J1,2 = 10.2, Hz, 2
H, H-1), 4.52 (br d, J6b,6a= 8.9 Hz, 2 H, H-6b), 4.48 (d, J1',2' = 6.4
Hz, 2 H, H-1'), 4.36 (dd, J6b',6a' = 12.5 Hz, J6b',5= 4.1 Hz, 2 H,
H-6b'), 4.07-4.01 (m, 4 H, H-6a, H-6a'), 3.74-3.67 (m, 4 H, H-4, H-5),
3.65-3.63 (m, 2 H, H-5'), 2.15, 2.05, 2.03, 1.99, 1.97, 1.94 (6 s, 42 H,
CH3). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 20.8, 20.9, 21.1, 21.3, 61.8, 62.4,
68.0, 69.8, 71.9, 72.4, 73.2, 73.3, 76.3, 77.1, 83.9, 101.2, 114.5,
115.3, 134.5, 142.8, 169.4, 169.6, 169.8, 169.9, 170.5, 170.7, 170.8.
HRMS (FT-ICR): m/z [M + Na]+ calcd for C60H72N2O34S2 + Na: 1451.3306;
found: 1451.33138. Anal. Calcd for C60H72N2O34S2: C, 50.42; H, 5.08; N,
1.96. Found: C, 50.16; H, 5.07; N, 1.91.
