$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of Diarly Sulphide (VIa-c) A solution of anhydrous sodium
acetate (0.01 mol) in ethanol (5 ml) was added to a hot solution of (IV)
(0.012 mol). An alcoholic solution of halonitrobenzene (V, 0.01 mol) was
then slowly added with stirring. The solution was refluxed for 4 hrs,
concentrated and cooled in ice over night. After filtration the solid was
washed with water until the filterate was colourless. Recrystallisation
from methanol afforded the desired product (VI). The physical data are
summarized in Table I. Compound: VIa, yield 70%. Molecular Formula:
C13H10N3ClS; M.p. °C: 193.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A convenient synthesis of 2-amino-5-methyl-3-nitrobenzenethiol and its
