$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Preparation of Diarly Sulphide (VIa-c) A
solution of anhydrous sodium acetate (0.01 mol) in ethanol (5 ml) was
added to a hot solution of (IV) (0.012 mol). An alcoholic solution of
halonitrobenzene (V, 0.01 mol) was then slowly added with stirring. The
solution was refluxed for 4 hrs, concentrated and cooled in ice over
night. After filtration the solid was washed with water until the
filterate was colourless. Recrystallisation from methanol afforded the
desired product (VI). The physical data are summarized in Table I.
Compound: VIC, yield 70%. Molecular Formula: C14H13N3O4S; M.p. °C: 233.
