solution of 4-hydroxythiophenol (151 mg, 1.2 mmol) and anhy. K2CO3 in dry
CH3CN (20 mL), 4-nitroiodobenzene (300 mg, 1.2 mmol) was added under N2
atmosphere and refluxed for 12 h. The workup yielded 208 mg (70 %) of
4-hydroxy-4'-nitrodiphenylsulfide.
