$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for the Thiocarbonylation-Arylation: Chamber 1: Aryl
diiodide (0.25 mmol), Pd(OAc)2 (0.234 mL stock solution, 2.5 mmol),
DPEphos (1.3 mg, 2.5 mmol) and NaOAc (45.1 mg, 0.55 mmol) was dissolved
in DME (0.766 mL). Chamber 2: 3.0 equivalents of CO were generated in
chamber 2. The glassware was then removed from the glovebox, and the
thiol (0.50 mmol) was injected into chamber 1 before mixing at 85 °C.
After 18 h, the solvent was removed from chamber 1 in vacuo and the
desired compound was purified by flash chromatography on silicagel using
a pentane/CH2Cl2 eluent system. S-Phenyl 4-(phenylthio)benzothioate (33)
as colorless crystals, yield 57 mg, 0.18 mmol, 70%. 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3) δ (ppm) 7.90 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 2H), 7.54-7.41 (m, 10H), 7.23 (d, J =
8.4 Hz, 2H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ (ppm) 189.1, 145.9, 135.1, 134.5,
134.1, 133.8, 131.8, 129.7, 129.5, 129.2, 129.0, 128.0, 127.4, 127.3.
HRMS (ESI) m/z calcd for C19H14OS2 [M+H+]: 323.0564, found: 323.0557.
