$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1-Propyl-1λ4-benzo[1,3,2]dithiazole 3,3-dioxide Compound 3 was prepared
in 60 % yield from 2-chloro-benzenesulfonamide according to the following
procedure: to a solution of potassium hydroxide (85%, 1.2 g, 20 mmol) and
n-propylmercaptan (1.81 ml, 20 mmol) in 10 ml DMF at 90°C was added a
solution of 2-chlorobenzenesulfonamide (1.91 g, 10 mmol) in 10 ml DMF.
The reaction mixture was heated to reflux for 5 h, cooled, and the
solvent was removed under vacuum. The residue was neutralized to pH = 7.0
by using 2 N hydrochloric acid and extracted with ether. The ether
extracts were combined, washed with water and brine, dried with MgSO4 and
concentrated under vacuum. The resulting residue was purified via silica
gel flash chromatography (eluents: ethyl acetate: hexane = 1: 1) to give
2-propylsulfanylbenzenesulfonamide (1.62 g, 70% yield).
