$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure A for Substituted Benzothiophene-2-carboximindine
Analogues (Scheme1). 2-Cyanobenzothiophene (3) Synthesis. To a solution
of arylaldehydes (1 equiv) in DMF (3 mL/mmol) and DBU (2 equiv) was added
thioacetonitrile (1.2 equiv) dropwise at 0 °C. The solution was stirred
at 0 °C for 20 min, then heated to 40 °C for 16-20 h. The reaction
mixture was allowed cool to room temperature, the solvent was reduced in
vacuo, and the product was purified via silica chromatography
(EtOAc/hexane mix), yielding the intermediates 3.
(2-Carbamimidoyl-benzo[b]thiophen-4-yloxy)-acetic acid ethyl ester (11):
Synthesised according to the general procedure A to give a beige solid
(11) (10mg, 9% ). 1H NMR (CD3OD, 400MHz) δ 9.02(s,4H, amidine),
8.28(s,1H,Ar-H), 7.57-7.53(m,1H,Ar-H), 7.34-7.26(m,1H,Ar-H),
6.78-6.74(m,1H,Ar-H), 4.86(s,2H,CH2), 4.00(d,2H,J=8Hz, CH2), 1.04(t,
3H,J=8Hz,CH3); MS m/z (ES+) 279.00 [M-H] Rt = 4.58.
