$DATUM Methyl 4-(Naphthalen-2-ylthio)benzoate (87).36 A mixture of
2-naphthalenethiol (78) (300 mg, 1.87 mmol), bromide 82 (400 mg, 1.86
mmol), Pd2(dba)3 (42 mg, 0.046 mmol), Xantphos (54 mg, 0.094 mmol), and
DIPEA (0.62 mL, 3.74 mmol) in dioxane (6 mL) was heated at 100 °C
overnight. The reaction mixture was diluted with EtOAc and filtered
through a pad of Celite, and the filtrate was concentrated in vacuo. The
residue was purified by flash column chromatography (hexanes/EtOAc).
Compound 87 as a white solid (10.6 mg, 2%). 1H NMR (CDCl3, 600 MHz) δ
8.03 (s, 1H), 7.90 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 2H), 7.87-7.83 (m, 2H), 7.82-7.78 (m,
1H), 7.53 (dd, J = 4.5, 4.5 Hz, 2H), 7.48 (dd, J = 8.4, 1.8 Hz, 1H),
7.27-7.23 (m, 2H), 3.89 (s, 3H). HRMS (ESI+) calcd for C18H15OS (M + H)+
279.0844, found 279.0849.
