$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To a benzene solution of 1 (4 mg, 8 micromol) was added
4-fluoroiodobenzene (4.5 μL, 40 μmol) followed by 2-thiocresol or
2,6-dimethylthiophenol (1.1 μL, 8.8 μmol). The red solution turned bright
yellow upon addition and brown within 5 min. n-pentane was added to the
suspension after 24 h at RT The liquid phase was evaporated to give a
reddish solid which was purified on silica gel column to yield the
corresponding biarylsulfide (from 2-thiocresol). The solid phase
contained complex 8. (4-fluorophenyl)(o-tolyl) sulfide, yield (2.0 mg,
95%); complex 8, yield (ca. 80%). (4-fluorophenyl)(o-tolyl) sulfide: 1H
NMR 7.26-7.22 (m, Ar-H, 3H), 7.20-7.10 (m, Ar-H, 3H), 7.02-6.98 (m, Ar-H,
2H), 2.37 (s, CH3, 3H); 13C{1H} 162.17 (d, JFC = 245.9 Hz, C-F), 139.09
(s), 134.91 (s), 132.86 (d, J= 8.1 Hz), 131.74 (s), 130.73 (s), 127.63
(s), 126.86 (s), 116.61 (s), 116.39 (s), 29.86 (s); 19F{1H} -114.48 (s);
EI-MS M+ (Calc. for C13H11FS) 218 (218).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
